"""Hingeboard (2026-11-06, LOOP.md G3; request: "make an app for my permanent keyboard on one screen -- that
keyboard app should change the orientation and function of the other screen", "the keyboard app needs to take over the
screen instead of pmos gui ... until the user exited it", "maybe the controller is a button on the on screen keyboard",
"so i can swap between if i am playing a game on the hdmi output").
A GTK4 layer-shell OVERLAY covering one whole screen (default DSI-1 = the screen without the camera), with NO keyboard
focus (keys go to the app on the other screen / HDMI), drawn for LAPTOP posture (rotated 90: hinge at the top).
Top bar: [mouse symbol = right click] [gamepad or keyboard symbol = one switch, shows the mode a tap goes to] [Phone/Exit].
  Keys     standard laptop layout -> a uinput keyboard (latching Shift/Ctrl/Alt/Super, Caps, hold = repeat)
  Gamepad  D-pad, A B X Y, L R, Select Start -> a uinput gamepad, multi-touch (hold several at once)
  Exit     closes the keyboard and puts both screens back to phone mode
While it runs there is ONE display: the other screen is Phosh's primary display (bars, home, app grid, apps) in
landscape (hingeboard-display-mode keyboard); this screen is only the keyboard. Exit (or SIGTERM) restores phone mode.
Run as the session user: hingeboard (it preloads gtk4-layer-shell itself).
Needs py3-gobject3, py3-cairo, py3-evdev, gtk4-layer-shell, wlr-randr; /dev/uinput writable by the input group."""
